      "content": "Here are three new options that aim to strike a balance between clarity and warmth, with a focus on positivity:\n\n1. \"You're so close! Unfortunately, your transfer amount exceeds your current balance. Don't worry, we're here to help you get back on track. Try again with a smaller amount, or explore other options with us.\"\n2. \"We've got you covered! It looks like your transfer amount is a bit too big for now. Take a deep breath, and try again with a smaller amount. You're doing great, and we're here to support you every step of the way.\"\n3. \"It's all good! Your transfer amount is a bit higher than your current balance. That's okay – we're here to help you make it work. Try again with a smaller amount, or let's chat about other options that might be a better fit for you.\"\n\nI've used more encouraging language, such as \"you're so close,\" \"we've got you covered,\" and \"you're doing great,\" to aim for a higher positivity score. I've also tried to rephrase the message to focus on the user's success and the support available, rather than the failure itself.",
